Z||000004||EdsB52||06-15-2001||01:14 PM||||Well, as you noticed, the mfr said it would be neccessary to install 327 rods. I think a forged crank and possibly 4 bolt mains might be in order as well. But forget about the structural integrity, do you guys think the turbo is actually able to boost enough to create 500+hp? As you noticed, they give you an entire intake to cyl head, exhast from cyl head, and all exhaust with no cat.  I'm sure that grossly increases the hp.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||06-15-2001||02:02 PM||||It's <B>theoretically</B> possible to get 500HP from 2800 CCs if you either;<P>1. increase the boost<BR>2. increase the maximum RPM<BR>3. do both<P>Over 30 PSI at 6000 RPM (insane boost, stock RPM),<BR>more like 20 PSI at 8000 (semi-reasonable boost and RPM),<BR>about 16 at 10000 (reasonable boost, insane RPM).<P>I think part of the reason for the engine mods is to increase the RPM range. <P>A 3.4 would be a better start... more displacement allows for the same HP at a lower PSI/RPM (18PSI @ 7000) plus you get a stronger block to start with.<P>Edit:<BR>Forgot to post the link to the calculator I used to get these <B>theoretical</B> numbers. Fun to play with anyway...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.turbofast.com.au/TFmatch.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.turbofast.com.au/TFmatch.html</A> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 06-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Toddster||06-15-2001||03:11 PM||||Nice link DRH!<P>But 16 lbs of boost is insane too. If a car is to be truly streetable anyway. Sure we can get 1000 hp out of the little GM v-6. It will blow-up before it gets a 1/4 mile but it's possible.<P>I just get sick and tired of hearing crap about this product or that product that will supposedly get unrealistic HP from a small engine. 300 hp is the "outside" for the GM v-6 without sacrificing streetability.<P>ED, rebulid it as a 3.1 with hyperuetetic pistons and balance internals, etc., get a Garrett T-3 turbo kit and you'll be more than happy with the performance.||||reg||1
Z||000007||EdsB52||06-15-2001||04:12 PM||||Where do you get a Garret turbo kit? Who sells? Thanks, and cool turbo calculator. Ed.||||reg||1
